    "body": "## Summary\n- Bind the mobile Battles tab label and accessible name to the renderer-owned `#battlesHeader .battleTitleText`, while retaining the live count.\n- Hide only the duplicate DM, Battles, and Events outer headers on mobile; preserve their DOM/counters and desktop presentation.\n- Handle touchstart/move/end/cancel gesture streams, arbitrate horizontal versus vertical motion, allow swipes over non-control card content, and suppress post-swipe clicks. Preserve controls, horizontal scrollers, closed panels, and Safari edge navigation.\n\n## Root cause\nThe swipe start filter treated whole `.battleCard` and `.eventCard` surfaces as interactive, rejecting horizontal gestures that began on card text. The tab label was static, and duplicate outer headers consumed mobile height.\n\n## Validation\n- `python3 tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py` (13 tests)\n- Browser HTML regression in the Codex in-app browser: PASS, including touch-shaped gestures on cards/buttons, vertical arbitration, closed DM, horizontal scroller, counts, five renderer-provided titles, desktop headers, and existing panel state.\n- `node --check` on both mobile controllers; `git diff --check`; Web/docs byte parity for all changed runtime pairs.\n\nThe DOM regression does not emulate native iOS Safari gesture recognition or physical iPhone hardware. Owner iPhone Safari retest remains required. No Safari PASS is claimed.",
    "changed_files": 8,
